result.summary:
PR #205 (CEIL14) is close to the brief and can go onto main as it stands. A few small test fixes would make it stronger. The merge base is 6fa2b52b, which is the REST1 commit itself, and neither OWNS file has changed on main since then (git log MB..main on Recruit.gd, the new test, Attrs.gd and AttrGen.gd returns nothing). The diff therefore applies cleanly to main today.

ceiling_of (scripts/rules/Recruit.gd:72-93) matches the brief line for line:
- the preloads and constants are added, and ceiling_of is added to the header list;
- the class bias is compared against the ability's PARENT, never the ability;
- the tilt comes from AttrGen.tilt_of, with a clamp of pot +/- 8;
- it reads with get only and never calls Attrs.of, sync or absorb;
- it returns minf(99, maxf(c, now + 2)) without rounding;
- ceiling() and every other function are unchanged, and nothing is wired into Sim, WeekPlan or Attrs.

There is no preload cycle: Attrs has no preloads and AttrGen preloads only Attrs. I re-derived the brief's numbers from TILTS, CLASSES and LEGACY and they are consistent: Out-boxer centred-tilt mean 1.62, Slugger mean 0.26, Ola 72.19/76/60/62/63.19, Rocco 90/78.37/74/85.87/77.87, nonsense 76/76/64/70.

The test (tests/ceiling_shape_test.gd, 83 lines) has exactly 7 _check calls (a to g). Each compares against the brief's numbers and returns -1 on main, so on main it would print failures=7. That is by construction only: no main-tree run was pasted. The dispatcher's headless runs report CEILING_SHAPE 7/0, RECRUIT PASS and PLAYTEST_S375 0, and CI's recruit_test passes. CI's only red tests are week_actual_test and guard_knee_test, which are red on main too and read nothing this PR touches.

Shortfalls:
- The PR body does not paste the 14 ceilings for Ola and Rocco or the main-tree run.
- The test does not print the population, and it prints only 7 of Ola's ceilings and 5 of Rocco's.
- The final line hardcodes checks=7.
- Check (d) does not pin speed 78.37.
- _c uses R.new().get_method_list() instead of R.get_script_method_list(). It works the same way and is harmless.
